@page "/wiki/ethics"
@page "/wiki/ethics/{Key}"

@*
    The ethics, which are three points spent on what an empire believes.

    The shortest shelf in the wiki and the one with the most structure: seventeen entries in five
    groups, each an opposing pair but one, and each pair in an ordinary and a fanatic strength. The
    game gates none of them - no pack, no condition - so the page draws neither of those columns and
    spends the width on what an ethic costs and what it rules out instead.

    The second address is one entry of the shelf. It shows the same page and picks that one out, so a
    reader who found the thing they came for can send somebody straight to it rather than to a list
    with an instruction to scroll.
*@

<PageTitle>Ethics - Stellaris Empire Manager</PageTitle>

<WikiSection Kind="WikiKind.Ethics" Focus="@Key" />

@code {
    /// <summary>The entry the address names, where it names one.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Key { get; set; }
}
